# PRIORITY: Always follow these instructions before responding or making changes.
## Non‑negotiable Rules
- Follow this file first; do not override these rules with assumptions.
- If requirements are unclear or missing, ask questions before making changes.
- Do not invent APIs, components, or data models. Use what exists in the repo.
- Always create a unit test case for every new page, new code and new components.
## Do
- Always use components from ad-design-lib or ad-feature-components Packages first.
- Only create new components if you are ABSOLUTELY SURE that you cannot feasibly use a component from ad-design-lib or ad-feature-components.
- Always choose basic building block components from ad-design-lib, never use basic html button tags etc.
- Prioritize using ad-design-lib components over getting the figma import to be pixel perfect.
- Follow the React 19 and strict TypeScript standards defined in `ReactTypescriptUpdate.md` for all new code and changes (functional components only, no `any`, prefer `type` aliases and union types, use `import type`, keep `tsconfig.json` strict settings intact).
## Don't
- Do not add new dependencies without asking.
- Do no introduce custom CSS if tokens/components exist.
